{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And there was darkness, pitch-dark.</b> Rashi's comment: that Israel saw their vessels and said, 'It is not in our power.' But this is difficult, for it is written, ״וה׳ נתן את חן העם בעיני מצרים וישאילום״ (and YHWH granted the people favor in the eyes of the Egyptians, and they lent them)." "<b>And there was darkness, pitch-dark for three days. And no man rose from under it.</b> Behold, that is six days. If so, the plague of darkness did not extend over a quarter of the month. And so it is in the Mekhilta: Rabbi Levi said: the seventh day of the plague of darkness — where was it? And he resolves it: HaShem stored it away for Egypt, for they were at the Sea, as it is written, ״ויהי הענן והחשך״ — which is rendered (in Targum): ״והוה עננא וקבלא למצראי״, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:58.482268633Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}